{"name":"April Fool’s Red","hex":"#1fb57a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fool","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person with poor judgment or little intelligence.","A jester; a person whose role was to entertain a sovereign and the court (or lower personages)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To trick; to deceive.","To act in an idiotic manner; to act foolishly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fool"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"April","blocks":[{"text":"April is the fourth month of the year in the Gregorian and Julian calendars. Its length is 30 days."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/April","wikidata":"Q118"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"},{"title":"April Fools' Day","blocks":[{"text":"April Fools' Day or April Fool's Day is an annual custom in many Western countries on 1 April consisting of practical jokes, hoaxes, and pranks. Jokesters often expose their actions by shouting \"April Fool[s]!\" at the recipient. Mass media can be involved with these pranks, which may be revealed as such the following day. The custom of setting aside a day for playing harmless pranks upon one's neighbor has been relatively common in the world historically."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Aprilsnar_2001.png/330px-Aprilsnar_2001.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/April_Fools'_Day","wikidata":"Q80949"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Breviarium_Grimani_-_April.jpg/500px-Breviarium_Grimani_-_April.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Breviarium_Grimani_-_April.jpg/500px-Breviarium_Grimani_-_April.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"April, Brevarium Grimani, fol. 5v (Flemish)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABreviarium_Grimani_-_April.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/36/Diamond.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/36/Diamond.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Faceted diamond","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADiamond.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Daisy_ntgr.JPG/500px-Daisy_ntgr.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Daisy_ntgr.JPG/1280px-Daisy_ntgr